{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-021",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 21,
  "title": "Job 21",
  "display_title": "Job 21",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 21,
  "sortOrder": 18021,
  "verseCount": 34,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "But Job answered and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Hear diligently my speech, and let this be your consolations.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Suffer me that I may speak; and after that I have spoken, mock on.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "As for me, is my complaint to man? and if it were so, why should not my spirit be troubled?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Mark me, and be astonished, and lay your hand upon your mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Even when I remember I am afraid, and trembling taketh hold on my flesh.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Wherefore do the wicked live, become old, yea, are mighty in power?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Their seed is established in their sight with them, and their offspring before their eyes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Their houses are safe from fear, neither is the rod of God upon them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Their bull gendereth, and faileth not; their cow calveth, and casteth not her calf.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "They send forth their little ones like a flock, and their children dance.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "They take the timbrel and harp, and rejoice at the sound of the organ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "They spend their days in wealth, and in a moment go down to the grave.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Therefore they say unto God, Depart from us; for we desire not the knowledge of thy ways.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "What is the Almighty, that we should serve him? and what profit should we have, if we pray unto him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Lo, their good is not in their hand: the counsel of the wicked is far from me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "How oft is the candle of the wicked put out! and how oft cometh their destruction upon them! God distributeth sorrows in his anger.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "They are as stubble before the wind, and as chaff that the storm carrieth away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "God layeth up his iniquity for his children: he rewardeth him, and he shall know it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "His eyes shall see his destruction, and he shall drink of the wrath of the Almighty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "For what pleasure hath he in his house after him, when the number of his months is cut off in the midst?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Shall any teach God knowledge? seeing he judgeth those that are high.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "One dieth in his full strength, being wholly at ease and quiet.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "His breasts are full of milk, and his bones are moistened with marrow.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "And another dieth in the bitterness of his soul, and never eateth with pleasure.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "They shall lie down alike in the dust, and the worms shall cover them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Behold, I know your thoughts, and the devices which ye wrongfully imagine against me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "For ye say, Where is the house of the prince? and where are the dwelling places of the wicked?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Have ye not asked them that go by the way? and do ye not know their tokens,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "That the wicked is reserved to the day of destruction? they shall be brought forth to the day of wrath.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "Who shall declare his way to his face? and who shall repay him what he hath done?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "Yet shall he be brought to the grave, and shall remain in the tomb.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "The clods of the valley shall be sweet unto him, and every man shall draw after him, as there are innumerable before him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:21:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "How then comfort ye me in vain, seeing in your answers there remaineth falsehood?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 21:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:21:34"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
